// CROWN — latency rides a GENERIC op RESULT instantiated at a fn:
// `give() -> a`, the arm resumes with a performing closure, the body calls
// it under `with !E`. Expect E_EffectMismatch.
//
// Checked clean and ran at 7 through the pinned boot (measured 2026-09-23).
// The result cap (`cap_result_fn_row`) reaches a DECLARED fn-typed result;
// a type variable that becomes a fn at the use has nothing to cap, and the
// op-result position flows handler to performer — the opposite direction
// from the parameter beside it (leak-op-param-generic-fn).
effect E { op() -> Int }
effect Give { give() -> a }
fn loud() = op()
handler g { give() => resume(loud) }
fn bad() with !E = {
  let f = give()
  f()
} ~> g
handler h { op() => resume(7) }
fn main() = bad() ~> h
